#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand parallel installs, which run isolated instances of the same snap "
"with separate names, data, configuration, services, apps, aliases, and "
"interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:8
msgid "Parallel installs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:10
msgid ""
"Parallel installs enable you to run multiple instances of the same snap on "
"the same system. Each instance is completely isolated from all other "
"instances, including its name, configuration, interface connections, data "
"locations, services, applications and aliases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:12
msgid ""
"Parallel installs are **enabled by default** from snapd 2.79. Earlier "
"versions of snapd treated them as an experimental feature that had to be "
"enabled explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:14
msgid ""
"Not every snap can be installed as a parallel instance. Snaps that use "
"unsupported interfaces or app properties are rejected when installed with an "
"instance key. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-unsupported>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:16
msgid ""
"To disable parallel installs, set the `experimental.parallel-instances` "
"system option to `false`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:18
msgid "sudo snap set system experimental.parallel-instances=false\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:22
msgid ""
"With parallel installs disabled, `snap install` fails when given an instance "
"key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:24
msgid ""
"The native package of snapd 2.79 ships new mount units, crucial for the "
"correct behavior of parallel instances of classic snaps. If you plan to use "
"parallel instances of classic snaps, see the [Classic confinement section]"
"(#classic-confinement) below for the required setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:26
msgid "Installing multiple instances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:28
msgid ""
"The process for installing multiple instances of a snap is identical to "
"installing a single snap except you *must* provide a unique identifier, "
"called an *instance key*, separated by an underscore (`_`) from the target "
"snap name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:30
msgid ""
"For example, the following command will install two instances of the [hello-"
"world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-world) snap with the second given an "
"instance key of `foo`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:32
msgid "sudo snap install hello-world hello-world_foo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:36
msgid ""
"To specify a specific {ref}`channel and track <explanation-how-snaps-work-"
"channels-and-tracks>` for each instance, install each instance separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:38
msgid ""
"For example, to install [Juju](https://juju.is/) 2.9 alongside Juju 3.0, run "
"the following commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:40
msgid ""
"sudo snap install --channel 2.9/stable juju_29 --classic\n"
"sudo snap install --channel 3.0/stable juju_30 --classic\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:45
msgid ""
"When installing from snap file, the instance key is set by passing `--"
"name=<snap>_<instance>` explicitly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:47
msgid "sudo snap install --name hello-world_foo hello-world_27.snap\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:51
msgid "Instance key naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:53
msgid ""
"The instance key needs to be manually appended to the snap name, and takes "
"the following format: `<snap>_<instance-key>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:55
msgid "For example, the following are valid instance names, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:57
msgid "`hello-world`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:58
msgid "`hello-world_foo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:59
msgid "`hello-world_0123456789`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:61
msgid ""
"Only lowercase letters or digits are valid, and the instance name can be up "
"to 10 characters long. After being set during the installation of a snap, an "
"instance name cannot be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:63
msgid ""
"ⓘ  The instance key **must** match the following regular expression: `^[a-"
"z0-9]{1,10}$`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:65
msgid "Instance management"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:67
msgid ""
"When working with instances, the vast majority of snap commands function "
"just as they would with a single snap. To remove an instance, for example, "
"use *remove*:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:69
msgid ""
"$ snap remove hello-world_foo\n"
"hello-world_foo removed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:74
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:76
msgid ""
"{ref}`Interfaces <explanation-interfaces-all-about-interfaces>` work across "
"multiple snap instances just as they do from any one snap to another. For "
"example, *xkcd-webserver* includes a *network* plug, as will all of its "
"instances, any of which can be connected to the system's *:network* slot:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:78
msgid ""
"$ snap connections xkcd-webserver_foo\n"
"Interface     Plug                             Slot           Notes\n"
"network       xkcd-webserver_foo:network       :network       -\n"
"network-bind  xkcd-webserver_foo:network-bind  :network-bind  -\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo snap disconnect xkcd-webserver_foo:network\n"
"\n"
"$ snap connections xkcd-webserver_foo\n"
"Interface     Plug                             Slot           Notes\n"
"network       xkcd-webserver_foo:network       -              -\n"
"network-bind  xkcd-webserver_foo:network-bind  :network-bind  -\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo snap connect xkcd-webserver_foo:network\n"
"\n"
"$ snap connections xkcd-webserver_foo\n"
"Interface     Plug                             Slot           Notes\n"
"network       xkcd-webserver_foo:network       :network       manual\n"
"network-bind  xkcd-webserver_foo:network-bind  :network-bind  -\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:99
msgid ""
"Slots provided by a parallel instance are never used for automatic "
"connections. If an instance provides a slot that another snap needs, connect "
"it manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:101
msgid ""
"sudo snap connect <consumer-snap>:<plug> <provider-snap>_<instance-key>:"
"<slot>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:105
msgid ""
"Some interfaces are not supported on parallel instances. See {ref}`Snaps "
"that are unsupported as parallel instances  <interfaces-parallel-installs-"
"unsupported>` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:107
msgid "Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:109
msgid ""
"As with Interfaces, {ref}`Services <how-to-guides-manage-snaps-control-"
"services>` function the same with multiple instances of a snap as they do "
"from any one snap to another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:111
msgid ""
"However, with multiple instances, you're more likely to run into port "
"allocation issues, such as two web servers needing access to port 80. In "
"such cases, only the service from one instance will be active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:113
msgid ""
"$ snap services\n"
"Service                            Startup  Current\n"
"xkcd-webserver.xkcd-webserver      enabled  active\n"
"xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver  enabled  inactive\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:120
msgid ""
"You can see why *xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver* is inactive by looking "
"at its logs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:122
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap logs xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver\n"
"2018-10-03T12:31:59Z xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver[1760]: OSError: "
"[Errno 98] Address already in use\n"
"(...)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:127
msgid ""
"As with single snap service collisions, the solution is to stop the service "
"on one instance and start the service on the other:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:129
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap stop xkcd-webserver.xkcd-webserver\n"
"Stopped.\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo snap start xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver\n"
"Started.\n"
"\n"
"$ snap services\n"
"Service                            Startup  Current\n"
"xkcd-webserver.xkcd-webserver      enabled  inactive\n"
"xkcd-webserver_foo.xkcd-webserver  enabled  active\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:143
msgid "Application names and aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:145
msgid ""
"Snap application names for multiple instances are adjusted according to the "
"following pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:147
msgid "`<instance-name>.<app>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:149
msgid ""
"When an application name matches the snap name, a short alias is created to "
"match the instance name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:152
msgid ""
"For example, with *hello-world* and *hello-world_foo* installed, *hello-"
"world.env* has an alias of *hello-world_foo.env* in the *_foo* instance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:154
msgid ""
"$ hello-world.env  |grep SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME\n"
"SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME=hello-world\n"
"$ hello-world_foo.env  |grep SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME\n"
"SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME=hello-world_foo\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:161
msgid "As with regular snaps, aliases can be added separately:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:163
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap alias hello-world_bar bar_env\n"
"Added:\n"
"  - hello-world_bar as bar_env\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo snap alias hello-world_foo foo_env\n"
"Added:\n"
"  - hello-world_foo as foo_env\n"
"\n"
"$ snap aliases\n"
"Command          Alias    Notes\n"
"hello-world_bar  bar_env  manual\n"
"hello-world_foo  foo_env  manual\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:178
msgid ""
"Aliases from instances generate conflict errors, just as they would with "
"distinct snaps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:180
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap alias hello-world_foo bar_env\n"
"error: cannot perform the following tasks:\n"
"- Setup manual alias \"bar_env\" => \"hello-world\" for snap \"hello-"
"world_foo\"\n"
"(cannot enable alias \"bar_env\" for \"hello-world_foo\", already enabled "
"for \"hello-world_bar\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:187
msgid ""
"When aliases trigger a conflict during snap installation, try passing `--"
"unaliased` with the command to disable automatic alias generation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:189
msgid "$ sudo snap install snap-with-conflicting-alias_foo --unaliased\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:194
msgid "Snap environment, data and namespace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:196
msgid ""
"When a snap application is run, its environment is populated with a number "
"of `SNAP*` environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:198
msgid ""
"The following environmental variables are potentially affected when "
"installing multiple instances of a snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:200
msgid "**SNAP_NAME**: the name of the snap, eg. `hello-world`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:201
msgid "**SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME**: the name of the instance, eg. `hello-world_foo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:202
msgid "**SNAP_INSTANCE_KEY**: instance key, eg, `foo` for `hello-world_foo`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:203
msgid "**SNAP**: location of files for the snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:204
msgid "**SNAP_DATA**: data for this particular snap revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:205
msgid "**SNAP_COMMON**: data shared between revisions of the same snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:206
msgid "**SNAP_USER_DATA**: user data for this particular snap revision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:207
msgid ""
"**SNAP_USER_COMMON**: user data shared between revisions of the same snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:208
msgid "**HOME**: user's home, equivalent to `SNAP_USER_DATA`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:209
msgid "**XDG_RUNTIME_DIR**: user's XDG runtime directory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:211
msgid ""
"For example, if *hello-world* and its instance, *hello-world_foo*, are "
"installed, the following name variables would be set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "snap"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "hello-world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "hello-world_foo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_NAME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_INSTANCE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_INSTANCE_KEY"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "foo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:219
msgid ""
"The data and mount points of parallel installed snaps are kept separate on "
"the host filesystem. Assuming the snap mount directory is `/snap`, the "
"following locations are used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "mount point"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/snap/hello-world/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/snap/hello-world_foo/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "system data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/var/snap/hello-world/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/var/snap/hello-world_foo/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "user data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "$HOME/snap/hello-world/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "$HOME/snap/hello-world_foo/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:228
msgid ""
"Within the mount namespace of a snap, adjustments are made to map instance-"
"specific locations to the snap locations. Taking *hello-world* as an "
"example, system data locations are set to the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_DATA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/var/snap/hello-world/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_COMMON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/var/snap/hello-world/common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:236
msgid ""
"However, due to security concerns, user data locations are *not* similarly "
"adjusted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_USER_DATA"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/home/<usr>/snap/hello-world/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:240
#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:241
#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:242
msgid "<usr>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/home/<usr>/snap/hello-world_foo/27"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "SNAP_USER_COMMON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/home/<usr>/snap/hello-world/common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/home/<usr>/snap/hello-world_foo/common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "HOME"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/run/user/<uid>/snap.hello-world"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:243
msgid "<uid>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "/run/user/<uid>/snap.hello-world_foo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:246
msgid "Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:248
msgid "Certain snaps, due to their nature, can never be parallel installed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:249
msgid "snapd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:250
msgid "core base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:251
msgid "kernel"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:252
msgid "gadget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:254
msgid ""
"All other snaps are subject to feature checking. Snapd checks every snap "
"installed with an instance key and rejects it if it uses a feature that "
"cannot work with more than one instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:256
msgid "Unsupported interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:258
msgid ""
"Some interfaces give the snap exclusive ownership of a system-wide resource, "
"such as a well-known D-Bus name. Others allow operations on shared hardware "
"or kernel state that would conflict if performed by more than one instance. "
"A snap cannot be installed as a parallel instance (unless specified with an "
"explicit bypass flag; see {ref}`Installing an unsupported snap anyway "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-bypass>`) if it declares a plug or slot for "
"one of these interfaces on an unsupported side:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "Interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "Plug supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "Slot supported"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`acrn-support <interfaces-acrn-support-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`adb-support <interfaces-adb-support-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`audio-playback <interfaces-audio-playback-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`auditd-support <interfaces-auditd-support>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`avahi-control <interfaces-avahi-control-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`avahi-observe <interfaces-avahi-observe-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`bluez <interfaces-bluez-interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid ""
"{ref}`checkbox-support <ref-checkbox-support-interface_checkbox-support-"
"interface>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:0
msgid "{ref}`classic-support <interfaces-classic-support-interface>`"
