#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:326
msgid ""
"When an instance cannot be installed, the error names the plug or slot "
"responsible and the reason, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:328
msgid ""
"cannot install snap \"network-manager_foo\" as parallel instance: slot "
"\"service\" with interface \"network-manager\" is not supported for parallel "
"instances: owning a unique global resource cannot have parallel instances\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:332
msgid "Unsupported app properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:334
msgid ""
"A snap is unsupported as a parallel instance if any of its apps set one of "
"the following properties in `snap.yaml`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:336
msgid ""
"`common-id`: the desktop file ID referenced by AppStream metadata is unique "
"on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:337
msgid ""
"`bus-name`: the well-known D-Bus name the app claims is unique on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:338
msgid ""
"`activates-on`: D-Bus activation requires a `dbus` slot, which is not "
"supported on parallel instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:341
msgid "Installing an unsupported snap anyway"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:343
msgid ""
"Users who understand and accept the risks of conflicts between instances may "
"bypass these checks with `--allow-unsupported-instances`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:345
msgid "sudo snap install --allow-unsupported-instances <snap>_<instance-key>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:349
msgid ""
"Snapd remembers this choice for the instance, so later refreshes are not "
"blocked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:351
msgid ""
"If a refresh introduces an unsupported plug, slot or app property to an "
"instance that is already installed and was fully supported, snapd blocks the "
"refresh and adds a warning visible with `snap warnings`. To refresh the "
"instance anyway, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:353
msgid "sudo snap refresh --allow-unsupported-instances <snap>_<instance-key>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:357
msgid ""
"`--allow-unsupported-instances` can only be used with snaps installed with "
"an instance key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:360
msgid "Interfaces that control shared system resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:362
msgid ""
"Some supported interfaces grant control over a resource that is shared by "
"the whole system, such as block devices or network ports. Each instance of a "
"snap that uses one of these interfaces acts on the same system resource, and "
"snapd does not coordinate between them. Before running more than one "
"instance of a snap that uses such an interface, make sure that the instances "
"are configured to manage different resources, or that only one instance is "
"active at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:364
msgid "Classic confinement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:366
msgid ""
"Snaps with {ref}`classic confinement <explanation-security-classic-"
"confinement>` can be installed as parallel instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:368
msgid ""
"Starting with 2.79, the snapd native package (deb, rpm, etc.) ships "
"additional mount units: `var-snap.mount` and either `snap.mount` (on Ubuntu, "
"Debian) or `var-lib-snapd-snap.mount` (on Fedora, Arch, openSUSE, and "
"others). The mount units must be active before installing parallel instances "
"of classic snaps. The units help establish the mount hierarchy needed for "
"ensuring that the automatically created `/snap/hello-world_foo/` to `/snap/"
"hello-world/` mappings do not interfere with the host's mount namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:370
msgid ""
"The `var-snap.mount` unit may need to be manually enabled for activation "
"during boot. The `snap.mount` or `var-lib-snapd-snap.mount` units should "
"auto-activate during boot if snaps are already installed, or upon installing "
"the first snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:372
msgid "Unit statuses can be confirmed by querying systemd, like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:374
msgid "Ubuntu, Debian"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:-1
msgid "active"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:-1
msgid "enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:396
msgid "Fedora, Arch, openSUSE, and others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:419
msgid "To enable the `var-snap.mount` unit, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:421
msgid "sudo systemctl enable var-snap.mount\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:425
msgid ""
"As mentioned in {ref}`the overview of parallel instances <interfaces-"
"parallel-installs>`, if your system previously did not have parallel "
"instances enabled but had at least one snap installed, update the native "
"package to snapd >=2.79, enable the `var-snap.mount` unit, and **reboot the "
"system**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:427
msgid ""
"The mount units are only needed for supporting parallel installed classic "
"snaps, and do not need to be active otherwise. For this reason, the mount "
"units are also not present on Ubuntu Core systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:430
msgid ""
"The mount units are not shipped with nor installed by the snapd snap. Users "
"of the snapd 2.79 snap still need the 2.79+ native package for the mount "
"units to be available on their systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:433
msgid "Current limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:435
msgid ""
"There are a few limitations with parallel installs that will be addressed in "
"subsequent `snapd` releases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:437
msgid "User data and runtime locations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:439
msgid ""
"The user data locations are kept separate across multiple instances. "
"Applications that hard code paths to either user data directories or the XDG "
"runtime directory may not function correctly as the AppArmor profile has "
"been updated to allow accessing instance specific paths only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:441
msgid ""
"Applications need to use `SNAP_USER_DATA`, `SNAP_USER_COMMON` or fallback to "
"using `HOME`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:443
msgid ""
"Applications built using most popular frameworks, such as Gtk/glib or Qt, "
"and that are already capable of observing both `HOME` and `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, "
"should continue to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:445
msgid "Ports, DBus names, shared memory and socket activation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:447
msgid ""
"Snaps may provide APIs consumed by other snaps or the host system at some "
"well known locations or addresses, such as DBus service names, /dev/shm "
"objects or semaphores, abstract socket addresses. While the default AppArmor "
"template has been updated to allow only instance specific access, connecting "
"interfaces may allow a wider access capabilities that can lead to conflicts "
"between instances of the same snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:450
msgid "Ports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:452
msgid ""
"When snapd installs a snap with services, the services are automatically "
"started. Services trying to bind to the same port may fail or function "
"incorrectly. Such snaps should deliver means for configuration of the "
"service via configure hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:454
msgid ""
"A demo snap https://github.com/bboozzoo/parallel-installs-demo provides an "
"example of reconfiguration via configure hooks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:456
msgid ""
"Repeated failed starts of a service due to a port already in use can trigger "
"systemd start-rate limiting and suppress further restarts. To avoid restart "
"suppression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:458
msgid "Identify the service name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:460
msgid "snap services <snap-instance-name>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:464
msgid "Clear the failed state before applying the new port configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:466
msgid ""
"sudo systemctl reset-failed snap.<snap-instance-name>.<service-"
"name>.service\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:470
msgid ""
"Apply the port configuration (this restarts the service through the "
"configure hook):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:472
msgid "sudo snap set <snap-instance-name> <key>=<port>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:476
msgid "DBus names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:478
msgid ""
"Snaps that own a well-known D-Bus name, through a `dbus` slot or the `bus-"
"name` app property, are not supported as parallel instances. See {ref}"
"`interfaces-parallel-installs-unsupported`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:480
msgid "Snaps with plug-side `dbus` interface declarations are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:482
msgid "`/dev/shm`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:484
msgid ""
"The default AppArmor profile allows instance specific access only. "
"Applications hardcoding paths can break."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:486
msgid ""
"The `shared-memory` interface is only supported on parallel instances for "
"plugs with the `private` attribute set to `true`, which gives each instance "
"its own private `/dev/shm`. Slot-side parallel installations with `shared-"
"memory` are not supported. Note that some interfaces such as `mir` allow a "
"wider access to `/dev/shm`. Such a snap would need to be updated to made "
"instance aware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:488
msgid "Socket activation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:490
msgid ""
"Snaps can use `listen-stream` socket definitions of three kinds: a network "
"address, or an `AF_UNIX` socket addressed by either a filesystem path or an "
"abstract name. Each behaves differently with parallel installs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:492
msgid ""
"**Network sockets** (for example a bare `<port>`) are not adjusted for "
"parallel installs. Instances trying to bind to the same address and port "
"collide in the same way described above under Ports. Since the address is "
"hard-coded, using `AF_INET`/`AF_INET6` socket activation is not recommended "
"for snaps that want to support parallel installs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:493
msgid ""
"**`AF_UNIX` filesystem-path sockets** using `$SNAP_DATA`, `$SNAP_COMMON` or "
"`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` for system daemons, or `$SNAP_USER_DATA`, "
"`$SNAP_USER_COMMON` or `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` for user daemons, are "
"automatically expanded to instance-specific locations, so the clients can "
"use the appropriate path, for example `/var/snap/hello-world_foo/common/"
"name.socket`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:494
msgid ""
"**`AF_UNIX` abstract sockets** must be declared with a `@snap.<snap-name>.` "
"prefix. When generating the systemd socket unit for a snap instance, snapd "
"automatically remaps this prefix to `@snap.<instance-name>.`, so each "
"instance listens on its own abstract address without colliding with other "
"instances. Clients must connect using the instance-qualified address, for "
"example `@snap.hello-world_foo.socket` rather than `@snap.hello-"
"world.socket`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../explanation/how-snaps-work/parallel-installs.md:496
msgid ""
"If, after any variable expansion or instance remapping, the resulting socket "
"address exceeds the maximum length of 108 bytes allowed for a [Unix domain "
"socket](https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/unix.7.html) address, snapd "
"fails to generate the socket unit and reports an error."
msgstr ""
